Subject: [PATCH] media: software HEVC decoding on Linux x64

The Linux x64 Chrome build compiles FFmpeg's HEVC decoder and parser and
uses them for HEVC Main and Main 10 video. A page can play H.265 video
without a hardware decoder, and canPlayType() and MediaCapabilities
report HEVC as supported. Other HEVC profiles are rejected. Builds whose
FFmpeg lacks the decoder keep reporting HEVC as unsupported.

